Continuing my GitHub Actions learning journey as part of my Cloud & DevOps roadmap!

📌 What is Workflow Run History?
Workflow Run History allows us to view and track all the executions of GitHub Actions workflows in a repository.
Whenever a workflow is triggered, GitHub records its execution details, including its status, start time, duration, jobs, and logs.
It helps developers and DevOps engineers monitor automation and troubleshoot pipeline failures.

🛠️ What I'm learning:
How to access the Actions tab in a GitHub repository.
How to view previous workflow executions.
How to identify successful, failed, and in-progress workflow runs.
How to inspect job details and step-by-step execution logs.
How to identify errors and troubleshoot failed workflows.

🔍 Common Workflow Run Statuses:
<escape>🟢</escape> Success: Workflow completed successfully.
<escape>🔴</escape> Failure: One or more required steps or jobs failed.
<escape>🟡</escape> In Progress: Workflow is currently executing.
Cancelled: Workflow execution was stopped.

💡 Key Takeaway:
Workflow Run History helps us monitor CI/CD pipeline executions, identify failures, analyze logs, and improve automation reliability.
